  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 7602.04 “Incident Command System” (ICS) means a standardized approach to the command, control, and coordination of on-scene incident management, providing a common hier",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 7602.04 “Incident Command System” (ICS) means a standardized approach to the command, control, and coordination of on-scene incident management, providing a common hierarchy within which personnel from multiple organizations can be effective. ICS is the combination of procedures, personnel, facilities, equipment, and communications operating within a common organizational structure designed to aid in the management of on-scene resources during incidents. It is designed for use in all kinds of incidents, from small to large and complex incidents, including planned events.\n\nSource. #13256, eff 8-24-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c7600.html"
